Troubleshooting Tips
Issue: Terraform apply fails with authentication error

Solution: Verify AWS credentials with aws sts get-caller-identity
Check that credentials have sufficient permissions for resource creation
Issue: IAM policy creation fails with EntityAlreadyExists

Solution: Delete existing policy or use a different name
Command: aws iam delete-policy --policy-arn <policy-arn>
Issue: Security group rules not applying correctly

Solution: Check VPC ID matches your created VPC
Verify CIDR blocks are in correct format (e.g., 10.0.0.0/16)
Issue: Python script fails with NoCredentialsError

Solution: Ensure AWS CLI is configured: aws configure
Verify credentials file exists: cat ~/.aws/credentials
Conclusion
This lab demonstrated essential cloud security practices for AWS infrastructure. You learned to deploy secure infrastructure as code using Terraform, automate IAM management with Python, perform security assessments, and implement defense-in-depth strategies. These skills are critical for maintaining secure cloud environments in production.

Key takeaways:

Always follow the principle of least privilege for IAM
Encrypt data at rest and in transit
Implement multiple layers of security controls
Automate security assessments and remediation
Enable logging and monitoring for all critical resources
Continue practicing these techniques and explore additional AWS security services like Security Hub, Inspector, and Macie for comprehensive cloud security management.
